This pull request addresses an issue where HorizontalLine and VerticalLine plottables would fail to render if the axis was inverted. The fix ensures that these lines render correctly even when axes are reversed.

## Changes Made

### HorizontalLine.cs

- Replaced the Range.Contains(Y) check with an inverted-axis-safe condition.
- Calculated the X bounds using Math.Min and Math.Max to ensure proper clamping, regardless of axis direction.

```
    public override void Render(RenderPack rp)
    {
        if (!IsVisible || !(Axes.YAxis.Range.Min <= Y && Y <= Axes.YAxis.Range.Max ||
                           Axes.YAxis.Range.Max <= Y && Y <= Axes.YAxis.Range.Min))
            return;

        double x1 = Math.Max(Minimum, Math.Min(Axes.XAxis.Min, Axes.XAxis.Max));
        double x2 = Math.Min(Maximum, Math.Max(Axes.XAxis.Min, Axes.XAxis.Max));
        Coordinates pt1 = new(x1, Y);
        Coordinates pt2 = new(x2, Y);

        CoordinateLine line = new(pt1, pt2);
        PixelLine pxLine = Axes.GetPixelLine(line);
        LineStyle.Render(rp.Canvas, pxLine, rp.Paint);
    }
```
> 💡 **Note:** While the second change (X bounds clamping) is not strictly required in this specific context—since `CoordinateLine` and `GetPixelLine` can handle unnormalized input—it was added to improve clarity and ensure consistent behavior if the logic is ever reused for filled spans or future rendering layers where coordinate order may matter.



### VerticalLine.cs

- Replaced the Range.Contains(X) check with an inverted-axis-safe condition.
- Clamped Y values using Math.Min/Max for consistent behavior regardless of axis direction.

```
    public override void Render(RenderPack rp)
    {
        if (!IsVisible || !(Axes.XAxis.Range.Min <= X && X <= Axes.XAxis.Range.Max ||
                           Axes.XAxis.Range.Max <= X && X <= Axes.XAxis.Range.Min))
            return;

        double y1 = Math.Max(Minimum, Math.Min(Axes.YAxis.Min, Axes.YAxis.Max));
        double y2 = Math.Min(Maximum, Math.Max(Axes.YAxis.Min, Axes.YAxis.Max));
        Coordinates pt1 = new(X, y1);
        Coordinates pt2 = new(X, y2);

        CoordinateLine line = new(pt1, pt2);
        PixelLine pxLine = Axes.GetPixelLine(line);
        LineStyle.Render(rp.Canvas, pxLine, rp.Paint);
    }
```
